# iso.tkr — the per-task ISOLATION channel (0.3.1 paralelizacao-eixo1-isolamento-por-task §5). A
# `task_reset()` at each simulated `#test` boundary clears a per-task Category C sink, so a reader test
# sees no residue whatever the order — the reshuffle-exposed leak cannot occur. The NATIVE member is
# the coverage sink (addressed by name through `scenario_true`); the intern sink is a C-route
# `Given source` case (env C — the intern builtins are staged off natively). TEST = the token, never
# the exit code (the axis law).

Feature: iso — a reset at each #test boundary makes both per-task readers hermetic

  # (iso_cov_no_leak, NATIVE) the function-coverage sink is a per-task member (E1-C1) that
  # `task_reset()` clears (E1-C2), one of the Category C singletons the NATIVE backend lowers directly
  # (`cov_mark`/`cov_distinct`). A writer test marks an id, a reader test counts the distinct marks,
  # and the two run in BOTH orders; because each test enters under `task_reset()`, the reader counts
  # ZERO in either order — the count does not depend on which test ran first, which is the hermeticity
  # the axis buys. NATIVE by construction: no env is declared, so the member runs on the default backend.
  Scenario: iso_cov_no_leak — the coverage reader counts zero in both orders, exposing no residue
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario iso_cov_no_leak: ok"

  # (iso_intern_no_leak, C ROUTE) the string-intern table is a per-task member (E1-C1) that
  # `task_reset()` clears (E1-C2), exercised down the C route where `tk_intern_get`/`tk_intern_put`
  # resolve (the intern builtins are staged off natively: `intern_put not yet lowered (N2)`). A writer
  # test interns "x", a reader test reads it back, and the two run in BOTH orders; each enters under
  # `task_reset()`, so the reader sees MISS in EITHER order. The per-task-ification and reset live in
  # the SHARED runtime, identical on both routes.
  Scenario: iso_intern_no_leak — the intern reader sees MISS in both orders, exposing no residue
    Given source = "cases/iso_intern_no_leak.tks"
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "iso-intern-no-leak MISS MISS"
